# Docker build context exclusions.
#
# The backend images (backend/Dockerfile, backend/Dockerfile.worker) build with
# the REPO ROOT as the context (their COPY paths are root-relative), so this
# file governs them. It keeps the context lean and — most importantly — keeps
# secrets and prebuilt local artifacts OUT of the image: the image installs
# from the lockfile and builds its own dist (SECURITY.md 4: no credentials in
# the image; supply-chain is the lockfile, not local node_modules).
#
# Applies to any future app image (web/admin) that shares the root context too.

# Version control + tooling
.git
.gitignore
.github
.turbo
.claude
*.log

# Secrets — never baked into an image (a local .env holds dev credentials).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local dependency trees — the image runs `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`.
**/node_modules
node_modules

# Prebuilt / generated outputs — the image builds these itself.
**/dist
**/dist-worker
**/.next
**/.expo
**/coverage
**/build
**/out

# Docs + evidence artifacts: not part of the runtime.
docs/
**/__tests__
*.md

# Prettier/evidence + lock noise the runtime does not need.
.prettierignore
**/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
